    "You cannot lead others further than you have led yourself. This foundational truth sits beneath every framework, every model, and every leadership theory ever written — yet most people who step into positions of authority skip past it entirely. They learn how to manage meetings before they learn how to manage their own impulses. They study team motivation before they understand what motivates them. They master external strategy before they understand their own internal patterns. This week begins where all real leadership development must begin: with you. Using Stephen Covey's Private Victory framework — the first three habits in his landmark work The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People — we will examine what it means to govern yourself before you govern anything else. We will also introduce Daniel Goleman's Emotional Intelligence model, which decades of research has shown to be a more reliable predictor of leadership effectiveness than IQ, technical skill, or formal education. By the end of this week, you will have an honest baseline assessment of your own self-leadership, and you will understand precisely why developing it is not a soft or optional exercise — it is the prerequisite for everything that follows.",
